{{also|Heathen}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|hethen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hǣþen}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*haiþin}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*haiþinaz|t=heathen, pagan|pos=adj}}, equivalent to {{af|en|heath|t1=heathland|-en}}. Cognate with {{cog|fy|heiden}}, {{cog|nl|heiden}}, {{cog|gmh|heiden}}, {{cog|de|Heiden}}, {{cog|de|Heide}}, {{cog|sv|heden}}, {{cog|is|heiðinn}}. See also {{cog|gem-pro|*haiduz}}, {{cog|non|heiðr|tr=honour, bright, moor}}, {{cog|is|heiður|tr=honour}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhiːðən/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-heathen.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːðən|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Not adhering to an [[Abrahamic]] [[religion]]; [[pagan]].
# {{lb|en|by extension}} Uncultured; uncivilized; savage, [[philistine]].
# {{alternative case form of|en|Heathen|nodot=1}} {{gloss|pertaining or adhering to the Germanic [[neo-pagan]] faith [[Heathenry]]}}.

