===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|heathen}} <!--see 1930 cite: you can have "two heathen"-->

# A person who does not follow an [[Abrahamic]] [[religion]]; a [[pagan]].
#* V. Knox
#*: If it is no more than a moral discourse, he may preach it and they may hear it, and yet both continue unconverted '''heathens'''.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1930|author=H. E. Bolton|title=Anza's California expeditions|volume=1|page=403
|passage=On hearing his cries two '''heathen''' who were hunting on the lagoon ran up, and they were bold enough to try to avenge the injury, making ready to shoot arrows at the soldiers, who fired two gunshots just to frighten them {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} An uncultured or uncivilized person, [[philistine]].
# {{alternative case form of|en|Heathen|nodot=1}} {{qualifier|an adherent of the Germanic [[neo-pagan]] faith of [[Heathenry]]}}.

